<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Onesilus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 497 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Onesilus of Salamis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Onesilus was the brother of King Gorgus of Salamis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> who, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, seized power and led most Cypriot cities into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-revolt">Ionian Revolt</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 498 BCE. He besieged Amathus, which refused to join, but was defeated and killed when a Persian army landed on the island in 497 BCE. The people of Amathus hung his head over their city gate.</p></div>
